invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem_lanes.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-vector
reason: the SSE2 split for the layers of span 2 leaves a's 32-bit lanes
  in their order, so lo and hi take the wrong pairs of a's coefficients
  into the butterflies. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the
  script builds bin/mlkem_vector_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    lanes a_even_first = _mm_shuffle_epi32(a, 0xd8);
--- new
    lanes a_even_first = _mm_shuffle_epi32(a, 0xe4);
